cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Nilpotent tridiagonal matrices with entries in {-1, 0, 1}: proof, Lean formalisation and computations"
authors:
  - family-names: Blattner
    given-names: Marcel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7188-673X"
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcelbtec/nilpotent-tridiagonal"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A classification of the nilpotent tridiagonal matrices with diagonal entries
  in {-1, 0, 1} and off-diagonal entries in {1, -1}: the pairs formed by the
  diagonal and by the products of opposite off-diagonal entries are obtained
  from the 1 x 1 zero matrix by two folding operations, one for each parity of
  the size. Nilpotent pairs of size n exist exactly for n = 1 and
  3 * 2^j - 1 <= n <= 2^(j+2) - 1, and then there are 2^floor(log2 n) of them.
  The proof rests on a rigidity statement modulo 4. The classification, the
  rigidity modulo 4, the admissible sizes and the count are formalised in
  Lean 4 with Mathlib. Python and C programs check all statements of the
  accompanying paper by exact computation.
keywords:
  - Bohemian matrices
  - nilpotent matrices
  - tridiagonal matrices
  - continued fractions
  - folding lemma
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
